<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειράς</span></b>  (Cret. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηράς</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>GDI</u>
			5024.19
		</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ridge of a chain of hills,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Ap.
				281
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				697
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Limen.
				22
			</span></i>; of the isthmus of Corinth, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				8.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>; of Trachis, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				491
			</span></i>: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				206
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγγει δ᾽ ὑπ᾽
				ὀφρύσι δειράδας,</span> of the petrified form of Niobe on
			Mt. Sipylus, which poured tears under the brow of the hill over its
				<i>ridges,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				832
			</span></i> (lyr.). (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δερσ-,</span> cf. Skt.
				<i>drsad-</i> 'rock'.)</div>
